{"name":"Polaris","hex":"#a0aead","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Polaris","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["α Ursae Minoris, a trinary star in the constellation Ursa Minor located near the north celestial pole for the last 1500 years.","A type of U.S. ballistic missile, capable of carrying a nuclear warhead and designed to be launched from a submarine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Polaris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polaris","blocks":[{"text":"Polaris is a yellow supergiant star in the northern circumpolar constellation of Ursa Minor. It is designated α Ursae Minoris and is commonly called the North Star. With an apparent magnitude that fluctuates around 1.98, it is the brightest star in the constellation and is readily visible to the naked eye at night. The position of the star lies less than 1° away from the north celestial pole, making it the current northern pole star. The stable position of the star in the Northern Sky makes it useful for navigation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ursa_Minor_constellation_map.svg/330px-Ursa_Minor_constellation_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polaris","wikidata":"Q12980"},{"title":"Polaris (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Polaris is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by writer Arnold Drake and artist Jim Steranko, the character first appeared in The X-Men #49, though she is not called Polaris until The X-Men #97. Dane has also been a member of the X-Men and the X-Factor, in which she is frequently paired with her on-again off-again romantic interest Havok."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Polaris_%282022_Design%29.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polaris_(Marvel_Comics)","wikidata":"Q2071256"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg/500px-Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg/1280px-Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg/500px-Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polaris components as seen by the Hubble Space Telescope","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APolaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/AlphaUMiLightCurve.png/500px-AlphaUMiLightCurve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/AlphaUMiLightCurve.png/1280px-AlphaUMiLightCurve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/AlphaUMiLightCurve.png/500px-AlphaUMiLightCurve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A light curve for Polaris, plotted from TESS data[29]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlphaUMiLightCurve.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Polaris_time-lapse_illustrating_Cepheid_type_variability.gif/500px-Polaris_time-lapse_illustrating_Cepheid_type_variability.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Polaris_time-lapse_illustrating_Cepheid_type_variability.gif/500px-Polaris_time-lapse_illustrating_Cepheid_type_variability.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content